Z||000000||chris6878||09-23-2000||06:33 PM||||Welp...   here goes...<P>I have an 85 SE v6...   it ran perfect till about a week ago..  and it started hesitating real bad...    will run a little while and then quit... but it made it home..<P>now i can start it fine and it will run about 30 seconds and then quit...  it seems to have a small miss also..<P>what could be going on?||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-23-2000||06:54 PM||||Thought they only made Fiero blues in 1987...?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Start with the basics:<BR>1) Ignition coil (perform ohmmeter checks outlined in Haynes manual).  No cost check.<P>2) Plug wires (especially, coil wire).  Check physical condition + ohmmeter check.  No cost.  <P>3) Rotor + cap. If they look OK, they probably are.    <P>4) Replace ignition module with an AC/Delco replacement.  Costs, but nice to have an extra one around. <BR> <BR>5) Keep us posted.<P>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
